# Keep the left-hand Thunderbolt xHCI out of runtime suspend.
#
# 0000:07:00.0 is the Alpine Ridge USB controller serving the two LEFT-hand
# USB-C ports (buses 3 and 4). Its PCIe PME wake path does not work: with
# power/control=auto it sits in D3hot and sleeps straight through a device
# insertion, logging nothing. That is why the left ports were recorded for
# years as "do not work at all" -- the silicon and the connectors are fine, the
# controller simply never wakes to notice.
#
# Forcing D0 makes it poll its own ports. A PNY drive then enumerates at full
# 10 Gbps SuperSpeed Plus.
#
# The right-hand controller (0000:7d:00.0) is already pinned this way by
# dock-xhci-recover, for a different reason.
#
# Cost: the controller never runtime-suspends, so a small constant power draw.
# Unmeasured, but a fraction of a watt against two usable ports.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", KERNEL=="0000:07:00.0", ATTR{power/control}="on", ATTR{d3cold_allowed}="0"
